 "summary_text": "In the 5-minute window, 11 visitors in 6 groups came in. The Camry drew the most interest: 6 of 9 passers-by stopped and 3 opened a door. But group g4 waited alone at the Camry for 4 minutes and then left without anyone talking to them. That was the costliest miss of the session.\n\nStaff took 74 s on average to make first contact, well above a 30 s target. The Song Plus converted well once someone sat inside, but the first approach still took 95 s.\n\nRecommendations:\n1. Put one consultant on the Camry/Tracker side during peak hours.\n2. Treat \"customer sitting inside a car\" as an instant cue to go over.\n3. Review the two unattended exits (g3, g4) at the next team briefing."
